WEBVTT

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:07.020
Puzzle No. J-319-H...

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:10.280
A puzzle was released once again, wasn't it?

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:13.660
This is the Solver chosen by the
Armlet of Orpheus, eh?

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:15.300
Kaito Daimon...

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.560
Can we continue to leave him be?

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:18.870
What are you trying to say?

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:23.750
He was able to solve a puzzle like this
in such a short time.

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:26.970
How do you think the head office judges the

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:29.290
command ability of us here in the Japan branch?

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:32.260
You're saying that how I'm doing things is mistaken?!

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:33.880
No, none of us implied...

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:38.590
You fools have no business saying such things!

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:39.930
I've taken steps to solve this!

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:43.350
Excellently done, Chief.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:45.350
Your words give us confidence.

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:49.300
<i>Just you wait:</i>

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.110
<i>Next time for sure, I'll send you straight to Hell,</i>

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:54.320
<i>Kaito Daimon!</i>

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:56.220
Look, look!
Whoa!

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:56.820
No way!

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:58.230
It's that celeb, Erena Himekawa!
No way!

00:00:58.230 --> 00:00:59.530
For real?!

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:02.090
You!

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:03.870
What the hell are you doing here?!

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:27.870
Kimi no nounai e to shinnyuu
Gonna infiltrate your brain

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:30.600
Nemutteru suki ni baby, open the gate
While you're sleeping, baby, open the gate

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:32.450
Fukuzatsusugi security
Too-complicated security

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:35.190
Kakusareru to abakitakunaru
When something's hidden, it makes me want to expose it

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:39.700
Barabara ni chirabatte iru password o hiroiatsume
I'll gather up those loose, scattered passwords

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:44.410
Kakushin ni sematte yuku, sono shoutai o misete
And approach the core, so show me that true form

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:46.630
Kantan ni clear dekinai
I can't clear it easily

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:49.280
Saki nante motto yomenai
Can read what lies ahead even less

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:51.290
Kaidoku fukanou smile
A smile that can't be deciphered

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:53.590
Kiken na puzzle
A dangerous puzzle

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:55.530
Lock sareteta door aru nara
If there's a door that's been locked

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:58.350
Zutto tataite miru beki, kaza-ana hiraku wa
You must keep striking it, a crack will open

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:02.850
Eien ni hodokenai nazo nanka wa nai
No mystery remains unsolved forever

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:05.150
Makiokosu, it's a supernova!
It's forming, it's a supernova!

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:09.840
Tobikiri shigekiteki na hirameki o agemashou
I will give you thoroughly stimulating insight

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:12.060
Misskey-misskey la-tu-ma

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:14.400
Yume no naka, it's a supernova!
In the middle of a dream, it's a supernova!

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.030
Watashi wa, sou, brain diver
I am, yes, a brain diver

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:22.920
Kimi ga sagashimotometeru kotae ni nareru made
Until I become familiar with the answer you seek

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:28.600
Brain diver

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:33.400
Brain diver

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:42.050
The Queen Strikes Back

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:48.280
At last, we shall have it!

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:50.850
Men, bring it out here!

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:00.030
Puzzle Guardian Fire!

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:03.860
Wh..What?!

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:06.710
That barrier will stand until you can solve the puzzle.

00:03:06.710 --> 00:03:08.190
That voice!

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:13.860
O those driven by greed:

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:16.210
I shall not hand this world's prizes to you!

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.880
I am the beautiful female warrior,
she of love and knowledge:

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:26.790
The Puzzle Queen, Erena!

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:31.410
Okay, cut!

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:33.360
Checking footage!

00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:38.380
What is this?

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:39.240
How should I know?!

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:41.240
Puzzle Queen Erena.

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:43.810
Puzzle Queen Erena?

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:48.250
It's Erena Himekawa's new,
post-Puzzle Kingdom show.

00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:52.780
This time, it's a sci-fi drama made for kids.

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:55.380
She creates puzzles and fights to protect

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:57.290
the world's treasures from evildoers.

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:00.840
Her barriers contain puzzles.

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:03.550
And if you can't solve them...

00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:08.260
Erena Thundercrash!

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:13.310
Okay, Mr. Monster, clear the way!

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:27.230
Hey, that's just like the Philosopher's Puzzles!

00:04:27.230 --> 00:04:28.980
So, Givers are the good guys

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:31.040
and we Solvers are the bad ones now?!

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:32.380
What a bunch of crap!

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:34.040
What are you so worked up about?

00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:37.540
Did receiving my invitation make you that happy?

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:39.710
What the hell are you schemin' this time?

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:41.000
Scheming?

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:42.840
That's not nice.

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:45.990
This is your reward for having beaten me last time.

00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:55.630
<i>If it stings that badly,</i>

00:04:55.630 --> 00:04:57.860
<i>then you should challenge them again.</i>

00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:01.390
<i>And you will defeat Kaito Daimon,</i>

00:05:01.390 --> 00:05:03.870
<i>along with all his companions.</i>

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:07.820
<i>There aren't any Philosopher's Puzzles
I'm in charge of anymore.</i>

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:09.700
<i>You should make them anew.</i>

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:13.210
<i>But I don't even have a prize to seal inside.</i>

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:15.710
<i>Then, perhaps you're fine as is.</i>

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:19.750
<i>You're fine having lost, pitifully, to the bonds</i>

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:22.100
<i>between Kaito Daimon and his friends.</i>

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:24.650
<i>I apologize for before.</i>

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:26.420
<i>I interfered with your plan.</i>

00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:28.710
<i>Next time, please do as you see fit.</i>

00:05:29.630 --> 00:05:31.340
<i>Puzzles!</i>

00:05:31.340 --> 00:05:33.850
<i>Were they once not everything to you?!</i>

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:36.090
<i>Without puzzles, what are you?</i>

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:38.520
<i>You are worthless, just a child!</i>

00:05:39.010 --> 00:05:41.640
<i>You must win.</i>

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:43.280
<i>You must.</i>

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:46.590
Hey, don't be lettin' your guard down.

00:05:46.590 --> 00:05:48.210
She's gonna come after us for sure!

00:05:48.210 --> 00:05:49.490
Yeah, I know th-

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:50.660
Kaito!
Yeah, I know th-

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:53.740
You two!

00:05:55.170 --> 00:05:57.240
They said I'm a "female warrior"!

00:05:57.240 --> 00:05:59.420
What do you think? Does it suit me?

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:01.360
She seems quite athletic,

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:03.590
so I graciously
offered her the role of assistant.

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:05.560
What's Ana's role?

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:07.310
I'm the Sacred Spirit of Puzzles.

00:06:07.310 --> 00:06:09.310
I, Ana, like these clothes!

00:06:09.310 --> 00:06:11.100
Have you all forgotten?!

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:14.190
She's a POG Giver!

00:06:14.190 --> 00:06:17.570
But she said she'd put us on TV.

00:06:17.570 --> 00:06:19.630
Besides, look at what you're wearing.

00:06:19.630 --> 00:06:21.210
That's different.

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:23.140
Huh? What the heck?

00:06:23.140 --> 00:06:24.460
Damn...

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:27.660
What? Is something strange?

00:06:27.660 --> 00:06:30.240
No, it's just, you...

00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:32.240
You look like Kintaro or some-

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:37.080
Well, I hope you all have fun.

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:37.080
I give up! I give up!

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:39.170
Hey, wait up, we're still-

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:41.040
Help me, Gammon!

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:43.900
It seems the Chief of the Far East Headquarters

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:45.590
has made another move.

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:50.070
He has always been surrounded
by dangerous rumors, but...

00:06:50.070 --> 00:06:53.090
His behavior is completely irrational!

00:06:54.030 --> 00:06:56.220
At this rate, Kaito and the others will...

00:06:57.080 --> 00:06:59.290
If limits are not crossed,

00:06:59.290 --> 00:07:01.600
one can never approach the Puzzle of God.

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:05.870
For the Phi-Brain children to be

00:07:05.870 --> 00:07:08.560
that much stronger, that much greater...

00:07:09.330 --> 00:07:10.890
For that purpose...

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:16.170
That damn Nonoha!

00:07:16.170 --> 00:07:18.760
What kinda trick will she try this time?

00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:22.580
Miss Erena, can you please check the puzzle?

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:30.350
<i>She can make good puzzles though.</i>

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:34.340
<i>Her... Her puzzles are-</i>

00:07:34.340 --> 00:07:35.620
What is this?!

00:07:36.140 --> 00:07:38.720
Here! This isn't what I specified!

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:40.340
Ah! I..I'm sorry!

00:07:40.340 --> 00:07:42.390
No more shooting till this is fixed!

00:07:46.870 --> 00:07:48.570
Quite the princess, aren't you?

00:07:48.850 --> 00:07:50.900
I can't allow mistakes.

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:53.570
Not in a shoot, not in life and not in puzzles.

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:55.720
Yeah, but still!

00:07:55.720 --> 00:07:58.080
I won't be defeated by some new show!

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:02.080
<i>You don't know what it's like to lose,
to feel misery in defeat!</i>

00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:04.220
<i>As for me, I...</i>

00:08:04.220 --> 00:08:05.940
<i>Erena Himekawa...</i>

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:08.090
<i>Think her time's about up?</i>

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:10.490
<i>She's cute, but she doesn't
have any real talents.</i>

00:08:12.860 --> 00:08:20.080
Puzzles

00:08:13.170 --> 00:08:14.710
<i>That's when it happened.</i>

00:08:15.480 --> 00:08:17.720
<i>Solving them was so easy, it was funny.</i>

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:19.720
<i>I had a gift!</i>

00:08:20.550 --> 00:08:23.580
<i>So, I used puzzles and made my way to the top!</i>

00:08:25.240 --> 00:08:28.120
<i>I won, I beat puzzles.</i>

00:08:28.120 --> 00:08:31.340
And I'll use puzzles to keep on winning!

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:35.720
To you, puzzles are just tools for winning, huh?

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:38.740
That's pathetic.

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:41.500
It's an insult to puzzles.

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:44.610
You don't make any sense.

00:08:44.610 --> 00:08:48.390
Fine, then what are puzzles to you?

00:08:53.060 --> 00:08:54.470
Important things.

00:08:54.470 --> 00:08:56.790
Important? What is that?!

00:08:57.490 --> 00:08:59.940
<i>I can't believe I lost to a sap like him!</i>

00:09:01.570 --> 00:09:02.690
Fine.

00:09:02.690 --> 00:09:05.830
Kaito Daimon, I will show you!

00:09:05.830 --> 00:09:07.980
You'll see my true puzzles!

00:09:08.310 --> 00:09:12.990
And I'll show you how to feel toward true puzzles.

00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:19.240
How to feel toward puzzles?

00:09:45.950 --> 00:09:49.130
Whoa, this is...

00:09:49.130 --> 00:09:51.050
A miniature set, huh?

00:09:53.430 --> 00:09:55.030
Welcome, everyone.

00:09:57.230 --> 00:10:00.160
I will now have you challenge my puzzle.

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:02.990
So, your "puzzle" is this mockup of the city?

00:10:03.270 --> 00:10:07.710
Yes, out of these buildings,
the blue ones can be moved.

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:09.810
If you carry them all over to

00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:13.580
that area and fill in the space, you will win.

00:10:15.470 --> 00:10:17.010
A 3D puzzle, huh?

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:19.170
There are fives types of shapes,

00:10:19.170 --> 00:10:20.790
and four different heights.

00:10:20.790 --> 00:10:22.930
You mustn't line them up at the same height.

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:25.190
And you can't place the tallest,

00:10:25.190 --> 00:10:28.080
eight-story building facing the river either.

00:10:28.860 --> 00:10:30.520
Your time limit is ten minutes.

00:10:30.520 --> 00:10:33.740
And "accidents" will occur, so it won't be easy.

00:10:33.740 --> 00:10:35.530
If you don't finish in time...

00:10:35.880 --> 00:10:38.740
Erena Thundercrash!

00:10:45.640 --> 00:10:46.780
This is...

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:51.410
So, when this reaches zero, we get burned to a crisp?!

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:53.330
What?! Where is it?

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:55.210
It's here?!

00:10:55.670 --> 00:10:57.520
These guys ain't involved!

00:10:57.520 --> 00:10:58.720
This is a fight against me, right?!

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:01.200
It's against you all.

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:03.220
<i>I'll take the five of you on at once!</i>

00:11:03.810 --> 00:11:05.120
You should be happy,

00:11:05.120 --> 00:11:06.970
being able to do your
precious puzzles with your friends.

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:08.080
Bitch!

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:09.230
Dai-moron!

00:11:09.710 --> 00:11:12.120
Let's teach her what happens when

00:11:12.120 --> 00:11:14.110
kiddies take their pranks too far.

00:11:14.390 --> 00:11:16.710
I'm gonna wipe that smug smirk off your face

00:11:16.710 --> 00:11:19.830
and grab that million yen off ya for sure!

00:11:19.830 --> 00:11:22.170
Money? There's no...

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:26.080
The prize isn't something so frivolous this time!

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:27.620
You're sayin' it's worth more than money?

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:28.650
Yes!

00:11:29.220 --> 00:11:31.120
There is only one of it in the world.

00:11:31.470 --> 00:11:33.420
But don't give it much thought.

00:11:33.420 --> 00:11:36.010
You will all lose to me.

00:11:36.010 --> 00:11:37.410
Shut up!

00:11:37.410 --> 00:11:39.130
There ain't no puzzle I can't solve!

00:11:41.830 --> 00:11:43.010
Preparations complete.

00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:45.090
I, Ana, will do the puzzle.

00:11:45.090 --> 00:11:46.790
I'll do it too!

00:11:46.790 --> 00:11:48.770
I won't be much help though.

00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:50.080
You all...

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:56.270
Puzzle time, let's begin.

00:11:57.130 --> 00:11:59.060
Puzzle Guardian Barrier!

00:12:11.180 --> 00:12:13.480
It's lighter than I expected.

00:12:13.480 --> 00:12:15.960
This will be easy, Kaito.

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:24.650
You all right, Ana?

00:12:24.650 --> 00:12:26.140
Thank you.

00:12:28.130 --> 00:12:30.440
Nonoha, that's the wrong way! It's backwards!

00:12:30.440 --> 00:12:32.910
Huh? But Ana said to put it this way.

00:12:32.910 --> 00:12:34.590
Cubik, it doesn't go there!

00:12:34.590 --> 00:12:35.930
Huh? But...

00:12:35.930 --> 00:12:38.000
Gammon, don't put it on the shoreline!

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:40.030
Shut the hell up, I was about to move it!

00:12:40.470 --> 00:12:42.100
But according to my calculations...

00:12:42.100 --> 00:12:44.660
I, Ana, think it should go like this.

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:46.780
That goes over there!

00:12:46.780 --> 00:12:48.030
Wait a minute.

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:50.690
This puzzle can be solved any number of ways.

00:12:50.690 --> 00:12:51.810
We don't have time.

00:12:51.810 --> 00:12:53.290
Just do it how I say!

00:12:56.110 --> 00:12:58.380
The two of us can lift a six-story building

00:12:58.380 --> 00:12:59.350
and an eight-story one, right?

00:12:59.350 --> 00:13:00.050
No prob!

00:13:01.020 --> 00:13:02.110
Don't lose your balance.

00:13:02.110 --> 00:13:03.050
Shut yer trap!

00:13:08.660 --> 00:13:09.950
Hang in there, Nonoha.

00:13:09.950 --> 00:13:11.440
No worries, no worries!

00:13:11.440 --> 00:13:12.060
Really?

00:13:12.060 --> 00:13:13.060
Yeah, leave it to me.

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:14.860
Just a little more, let's go!

00:13:23.910 --> 00:13:25.280
What's that?!

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:33.040
A UFO? A UFO?!

00:13:33.190 --> 00:13:34.830
What the hell is that?

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:36.400
I told you, didn't I?

00:13:36.400 --> 00:13:38.750
That there would be accidents?

00:13:49.700 --> 00:13:51.260
Are you all right, Cube?

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:52.720
It's "Cubik"!

00:13:59.210 --> 00:14:01.230
Ah, the UFO!

00:14:01.230 --> 00:14:03.360
At this rate, we can't even move!

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:05.150
Let everyone else go!

00:14:05.790 --> 00:14:08.430
This will be between us, one on one!

00:14:08.430 --> 00:14:10.200
You should have had enough time.

00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:12.700
If you hadn't worked apart at first, that is.

00:14:12.790 --> 00:14:15.910
If you wish to save your comrades,
why not simply give up?

00:14:16.370 --> 00:14:19.170
Your precious friends will be the cause of your defeat!

00:14:32.980 --> 00:14:34.560
Huh? What?

00:14:38.820 --> 00:14:41.480
They're filled with real explosives!

00:14:42.830 --> 00:14:45.340
Dammit, Erena!

00:14:45.340 --> 00:14:47.470
No, I didn't do-

00:15:00.770 --> 00:15:02.390
<i>At this rate...</i>

00:15:08.750 --> 00:15:11.430
<i>This... This isn't my puzzle!</i>

00:15:12.600 --> 00:15:13.930
The POG, huh?

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:15.410
Kaito!

00:15:17.960 --> 00:15:19.180
Yeah!

00:15:22.420 --> 00:15:24.210
Take this!

00:15:25.060 --> 00:15:25.860
Nonoha!

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:27.390
All right!

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:39.610
My... My puzzle!

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:44.380
The controller!

00:15:46.230 --> 00:15:48.050
Safe!

00:15:51.890 --> 00:15:52.770
Nonoha!

00:15:52.770 --> 00:15:54.120
All right!

00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:56.100
This makes the last one!

00:15:58.180 --> 00:15:59.570
Thank you, Nonoha!

00:15:59.570 --> 00:16:00.850
Galileo...

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:02.600
Why?

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:06.110
Jeez, you sure are a meddlin' princess, ain't ya?

00:16:10.340 --> 00:16:11.860
We're outta time!

00:16:12.170 --> 00:16:15.150
Erena, take off everyone's explosives.

00:16:15.150 --> 00:16:17.380
I can't; the controller's gone!

00:16:17.970 --> 00:16:21.760
This wasn't the kind of puzzle I wanted to make!

00:16:21.760 --> 00:16:24.280
I won't let a puzzle kill people.

00:16:29.430 --> 00:16:31.930
B..But what can you...

00:16:34.530 --> 00:16:36.420
What I've learned so far:

00:16:36.420 --> 00:16:39.680
Gammon and I can lift ten stories' worth on our own.

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:41.110
Nonoha can do eight stories,

00:16:41.110 --> 00:16:43.190
Ana and Cubik two stories.

00:16:43.190 --> 00:16:46.690
No matter what we do,
someone will have to make three trips.

00:16:47.080 --> 00:16:49.130
That means, time will run out.

00:16:52.100 --> 00:16:52.950
But...

00:16:53.510 --> 00:16:55.150
Cubik has that.

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:56.920
I see it.

00:17:54.420 --> 00:17:55.620
You solved it.

00:17:57.430 --> 00:17:59.010
I'm so glad you solved it!

00:18:16.210 --> 00:18:18.320
Hey, these are...

00:18:18.320 --> 00:18:20.990
They're all wrong, aren't they?

00:18:21.010 --> 00:18:23.850
Puzzles
Erena

00:18:21.960 --> 00:18:23.360
"Erena"?

00:18:23.360 --> 00:18:25.530
Erena, this is your puzzle book?

00:18:25.530 --> 00:18:27.350
From when you were young?

00:18:27.350 --> 00:18:29.920
But you said you solved them easily.

00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:31.060
That was a lie.

00:18:31.060 --> 00:18:33.190
At first, I couldn't solve them at all.

00:18:33.190 --> 00:18:35.540
That's the past I wanted to erase.

00:18:35.540 --> 00:18:38.840
If that book got out, it would cause
an uproar with management.

00:18:38.840 --> 00:18:40.850
A lot of people would want that.

00:18:40.850 --> 00:18:42.830
If you sold it, you could get a million yen or more.

00:18:44.750 --> 00:18:47.400
I had nothing else that could act as a prize.

00:18:47.400 --> 00:18:49.710
A pure, straightforward line.

00:18:51.230 --> 00:18:54.500
Yeah, the same as your puzzles.

00:18:54.500 --> 00:18:57.570
Though that gets hidden by traps and gimmicks.

00:18:57.570 --> 00:18:59.970
This is the real you.

00:18:59.970 --> 00:19:02.780
The real me?

00:19:03.360 --> 00:19:06.450
You've wanted someone to solve your puzzles.

00:19:06.450 --> 00:19:08.870
Wanted them to notice the real you.

00:19:18.680 --> 00:19:20.520
<i>Wait, Mama!</i>

00:19:20.520 --> 00:19:21.550
<i>Mama!</i>

00:19:32.190 --> 00:19:35.030
I was happy that I could solve puzzles.

00:19:38.880 --> 00:19:42.160
I was so happy that I wanted to make my own.

00:19:42.560 --> 00:19:44.480
And everyone else was happy.

00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:47.770
I didn't want to lose ever again,

00:19:47.770 --> 00:19:50.010
so I had to keep winning.

00:19:52.730 --> 00:19:53.850
But...

00:19:58.680 --> 00:20:00.340
When you look at a puzzle,

00:20:00.340 --> 00:20:02.420
you know the heart of the person who made it.

00:20:02.420 --> 00:20:05.050
That's how to feel toward puzzles?

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:08.020
You didn't "beat" the puzzles.

00:20:08.740 --> 00:20:10.560
You were supported by them.

00:20:10.750 --> 00:20:13.660
This is your true prize.

00:20:14.540 --> 00:20:16.440
Don't let go of what's important.

00:20:17.140 --> 00:20:18.450
Never.

00:20:21.650 --> 00:20:24.610
The feeling toward puzzles, eh?

00:20:24.610 --> 00:20:26.780
I'll have to research that when I get back.

00:20:27.140 --> 00:20:29.350
Trying to act all cool...

00:20:29.350 --> 00:20:31.360
Shut your yap, Kinta-

00:20:33.880 --> 00:20:37.080
Next time, you'll put a real prize in there, right?

00:20:37.080 --> 00:20:38.340
You're good friends.

00:20:38.340 --> 00:20:42.980
Jeez! Well, as a Solver, I guess you'd be okay.

00:20:42.980 --> 00:20:45.430
You're quite good too.

00:20:46.200 --> 00:20:48.930
Not that you hold a candle to me, of course.

00:20:54.550 --> 00:20:57.610
"Puzzle time, let's begin," he says?!

00:21:03.860 --> 00:21:07.280
Damn you, Kaito Daimon!

00:21:07.280 --> 00:21:10.730
You've made me genuinely angry!

00:21:10.730 --> 00:21:13.690
But the game ends here.

00:21:13.690 --> 00:21:15.230
Now, you will die!

00:21:17.100 --> 00:21:18.460
That's enough.

00:21:23.280 --> 00:21:24.250
Bastard!

00:21:27.400 --> 00:21:28.890
Rook!

00:21:28.890 --> 00:21:33.100
This time, you were filmed from start to finish.

00:21:34.580 --> 00:21:37.170
You interfered in a puzzle made by a Giver,

00:21:37.170 --> 00:21:38.960
and tried to eliminate the

00:21:38.960 --> 00:21:41.150
Solver Kaito Daimon via unjust means.

00:21:41.720 --> 00:21:44.150
We have already submitted our
report to the head office.

00:21:44.150 --> 00:21:47.420
Shut up! I'm Chief of the Far East Headquarters!

00:21:47.420 --> 00:21:49.590
You bastards are-

00:21:51.570 --> 00:21:54.580
That... That's an officer's badge!

00:21:54.580 --> 00:21:58.000
Don't tell me you're assigned directly
to Count Pythagoras!

00:21:58.330 --> 00:22:02.250
The count has given Mr. Rook
complete discretionary control.

00:22:03.890 --> 00:22:05.990
Wh..What are you doing?!

00:22:05.010 --> 00:22:06.980
Your role in this has ended.

00:22:05.990 --> 00:22:08.310
Let go! Let go, now!

00:22:06.980 --> 00:22:08.130
Goodbye.

00:22:08.130 --> 00:22:10.550
Eliminating Kaito Daimon was an order

00:22:10.550 --> 00:22:12.500
from the head office, was it not?!

00:22:12.500 --> 00:22:15.370
I simply obeyed!

00:22:15.370 --> 00:22:18.170
The count! Let me speak to the count!

00:22:18.170 --> 00:22:19.570
Rook!

00:22:21.230 --> 00:22:24.530
<i>You take everything on and you solve the puzzle.</i>

00:22:25.330 --> 00:22:26.550
<i>You've gotten stronger.</i>

00:22:27.160 --> 00:22:28.970
<i>Soon, it will be puzzle time with me.</i>

00:22:29.840 --> 00:22:31.030
<i>Let's begin.</i>

00:22:37.270 --> 00:22:41.490
Tsukue no ue de umareta sekai
A world born on top of a desk

00:22:41.490 --> 00:22:47.410
Ichiban saki ni kimi ni misetakatta
I wanted to show it to you first of all

00:22:47.410 --> 00:22:52.040
Karappo no heya sotto nukedashite
I sneaked silently out of that empty room

00:22:52.040 --> 00:22:57.090
Hashirihajimeteta
And started running

00:22:58.250 --> 00:23:02.570
Iki hazumasete oka o noboru to
Breathing heavily, I climbed the hill

00:23:02.570 --> 00:23:07.930
Kimi ga saki ni tsuite matte ita ne
And you were already there, waiting

00:23:08.800 --> 00:23:13.110
Takusan no hajimete kimi to mitsuketa
There were so many treasures that I first

00:23:13.110 --> 00:23:18.360
Takaramono datta
Discovered with you

00:23:18.360 --> 00:23:23.700
Kanashisa de afureta toki wa
That time when I was overcome with sadness

00:23:23.700 --> 00:23:26.380
Nanimo iwazu ni tada
You said nothing

00:23:26.380 --> 00:23:29.290
Soba ni ite kureta ne
Just stayed there by my side, didn't you?

00:23:29.290 --> 00:23:33.860
Imademo wasurenai yo
Even now, I haven't forgotten

00:23:33.860 --> 00:23:39.160
Mata aou ne, yakusoku o shiyou
Let's meet again, let's make it a promise

00:23:39.160 --> 00:23:44.440
Kei wa shinai, ano hi no sayonara
It won't fade, the "goodbye" of that day

00:23:44.440 --> 00:23:49.980
Boku no subete, kimi ga kureta michi
Everything I have, the path you gave me

00:23:49.980 --> 00:23:58.920
Zutto kokoro no naka hikaru yo
Will always shine within my heart

00:24:04.080 --> 00:24:08.150
Rook, I never thought I'd see you again!

00:24:08.150 --> 00:24:11.510
It's been nine years, but you haven't changed a bit!

00:24:12.760 --> 00:24:14.910
I ain't never forgot the days that you, me

00:24:14.910 --> 00:24:17.010
and that guy used to spend together.

00:24:17.010 --> 00:24:19.770
Let's have fun again, like we used to do back then!

00:24:19.770 --> 00:24:22.440
Next time: "Puzzle Time at Reunion"

00:24:21.540 --> 00:24:27.250
Puzzle Time at Reunion

00:24:22.970 --> 00:24:26.520
Those were special times for me, Rook.
